ProductDetails.razor:

```razor
@page "/products/{Id:int}"

<h1>Product @Id</h1>

@code {
    [Parameter] public int Id { get; set; }
}
```

No other page has a route that starts with `/products`. The user types `/products/abc` in the address bar.

**What happens?**

ProductDetails.razor (interactive):

```razor
@page "/products/{Id:int}"

<h1>@title</h1>
<p>Id: @Id</p>
<a href="products/@(Id + 1)">Next</a>

@code {
    [Parameter] public int Id { get; set; }
    private string title = "";

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        title = $"Product {Id}";
    }
}
```

The user opens `/products/1`, then clicks **Next**.

**What does the page show now?**

Search.razor:

```razor
@page "/search"

<p>Results for @Q, page @(Page ?? 1)</p>

@code {
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery] public string? Q { get; set; }
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "p")] public int? Page { get; set; }
}
```

The user opens `/search?q=cats&page=3`.

